Delivery of the equipment is expected in December 2026.</p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify">&#160;</p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify">The impairment loss on prepayments is recognized within
general and administrative expenses in the consolidated statements of income and comprehensive income. During the six months ended June
30, 2025 and 2026, the Company recorded no impairment loss on its prepayments.</p>

